1
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:27,000
The lucky ones die first.

2
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:48,000
The Hills Have Eyes is a horror, thriller film directed by Alexandre Aja.

3
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:09,000
Based on Wes Craven's 1977 suspenseful cult classic, The Hills Have Eyes is the story of a family road trip
that goes terrifyingly awry when the travelers become stranded in a government atomic zone.

4
00:21:24,000 --> 00:21:30,000
Miles from nowhere, the Carter family soon realizes the seemingly uninhabited wasteland is
actually the breeding ground of a blood-thirsty mutant family...and they are the prey.

5
00:26:45,000 --> 00:26:51,000
Lynn, played by Vinessa Shaw.

6
00:32:06,000 --> 00:32:12,000
Doug, played by Aaron Stanford.

7
00:37:27,000 --> 00:37:33,000
Big Bob, played by Ted Levine.

8
00:42:48,000 --> 00:42:54,000
Ethel, played by Kathleen Quinlan.

9
00:48:09,000 --> 00:48:15,000
Brenda, played by Emilie de Ravin.

10
00:53:30,000 --> 00:53:36,000
Bobby, played by Dan Byrd.

11
00:58:51,000 --> 00:58:57,000
The Hills Have Eyes is a 2006 American horror film directed by Alexandre Aja and
co-written by Aja and Grégory Levasseur, in their English-language debut.

12
01:04:12,000 --> 01:04:18,000
It is a remake of Wes Craven's 1977 film of the same name.

13
01:09:33,000 --> 01:09:39,000
The film stars Aaron Stanford, Kathleen Quinlan, Vinessa Shaw, Emilie de Ravin, Dan Byrd, Robert Joy, and Ted Levine, and
follows a family that is targeted by a group of cannibalistic mutants after their car breaks down in the desert.

14
01:14:54,000 --> 01:15:00,000
The Hills Have Eyes was released theatrically in the United
States and United Kingdom on March 10, 2006.

15
01:20:15,000 --> 01:20:21,000
It earned $15.5 million in its opening weekend in the United States, where it was originally rated
NC-17 for strong, gruesome violence, but was later edited down to achieve an R rating.

16
01:25:36,000 --> 01:25:42,000
An unrated DVD version was released on June 20, 2006.

17
01:30:57,000 --> 01:31:03,000
A sequel, The Hills Have Eyes 2, was released in 2007.

18
01:36:18,000 --> 01:36:24,000
The film explores themes of van, rape, ambush, gas station, new mexico.

19
01:41:39,000 --> 01:41:45,000
The tone is dark and intense.
